/Title (Together, similarity and dissimilarity are called proximity - a numerical measure of how alike \(or unalike\) two data objects are. Dissimilarity is the degree to which two objects differ, usually expressed in the range [0,1] or sometimes [0, infinity\). Similarity is the degree to which two objects are alike, usually non-negative and often in [0,1], with 0 meaning completely unalike and 1 meaning identical. The proximity between two objects is built up from the proximity between their corresponding individual attributes. )
