/Title (Proximity measures are not a niche mathematical curiosity - they are the computational core of several major machine learning tasks: clustering \(grouping similar ShopCart customers into segments without labels\), nearest-neighbour classification and recommendation, anomaly detection \(flagging points that are dissimilar to everything else\), and information retrieval \(ranking documents by similarity to a query\). Some methods, called kernel methods, go even further - they transform raw data straight into a similarity space and never look back at the original attributes. )
