/Title (No: cosine similarity is invariant to positive scaling, so the currency conversion \(a pure multiplicative rescale\) does not change the answer - it would change only if the transform included an offset, exactly as in the Fahrenheit case above. The same logic applies to height \(centimeters vs. inches\) or weight \(kilograms vs. pounds\): any pure unit rescaling leaves cosine and correlation unchanged, but not Euclidean distance. )
