906 0 obj
<<
/Title (Only one of the four toy dimensions is sensitive to lighting, yet because Euclidean distance sums squared differences across all dimensions equally, that single dimension dominates the total and produces exactly the wrong ranking: d\(A normal, A different light\) = 2.85, larger than d\(A normal, B\) = 1.366, even though A and B are different people. )
/Dest [22 0 R /XYZ 72.177246 131.262695 0]
/Parent 4 0 R
/SE 138 0 R
/Prev 904 0 R
/Next 908 0 R
>>
endobj
907 0 obj
<<
/Title (Correlation is completely blind to non-linear structure. The relationship y = x squared is perfectly deterministic - knowing x tells you y exactly - yet its Pearson correlation is approximately zero, because the relationship curves rather than trending consistently up or down. )
/Dest [26 0 R /XYZ 72.177246 628.68945 0]
/Parent 4 0 R
/SE 167 0 R
/Prev 909 0 R
/Next 905 0 R
>>
endobj
