911 0 obj
<<
/Title (ShopCart's kitchen-appliance category shows the same pattern in real sales logs: hotter days, more ice-cream makers sold. A correlation of 1 \(or -1\) means a perfect positive \(or negative\) linear relationship, i.e., one variable is exactly an affine function of the other. )
/Dest [26 0 R /XYZ 72.381348 716.82568 0]
/Parent 4 0 R
/SE 165 0 R
/Prev 913 0 R
/Next 909 0 R
>>
endobj
912 0 obj
<<
/Title (Plotting income against spend for a population of ShopCart customers, Euclidean distance contours are circles - they treat every direction as equally far from a reference point. Mahalanobis contours are ellipses that stretch along the natural income/spend trend. As a result, a customer who breaks that trend registers as far more unusual under Mahalanobis distance than a customer who simply sits further along the trend, even though both customers might sit on the same Euclidean ring around the center. )
/Dest [23 0 R /XYZ 72.177246 267.58887 0]
/Parent 4 0 R
/SE 150 0 R
/Prev 910 0 R
/Next 914 0 R
>>
endobj
913 0 obj
<<
